# World VFX (Echo and Shared Paths)

**`main`-mod** concern (`EchoBoss` / adapters; not in base `master`). Any combat, ability, spell, item, or move that shows world VFX must work for **Hero and on-stage Echo**. Gate on sprite-attached-to-scene, not “is this the player”. There is no `UseContext` / `heroFX` flag.

## Gate correctly

| Concern                                                                       | Gate                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      |
| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Attack, jump, zap, missiles, operate, emitters, hit sounds for those          | [`Char.canWorldFx`](core/src/main/java/com/shatteredpixel/shatteredpixeldungeon/actors/Char.java)`(ch)` / [`EchoActionContext.canWorldFx()`](core/src/main/java/com/shatteredpixel/shatteredpixeldungeon/heroechoes/action/EchoActionContext.java) (`sprite != null && parent != null`) — pass the **body**; the kit mirrors the body's sprite, so either works, but the body is the char that is actually on stage |
| QuickSlot, GLog, identify, talent UI, `spendAndNext`, camera-only Hero riders | Hero entry points only. Echo adapters skip these.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         |

```java
// ❌ BAD — Echo never swings / never bolts
if (ch == Dungeon.hero && ch.sprite != null) {
	ch.sprite.attack(enemy.pos, doHit);
} else {
	doHit.call();
}

// ✅ GOOD — on-stage char: visual then hit; headless: sync only
if (Char.canWorldFx(ch)) {
	ch.sprite.attack(enemy.pos, doHit);
} else {
	doHit.call();
}
```

Echo adapters: `EchoActionContext.of(boss)` then `ctx.canWorldFx()`. The kit's sprite is **mirrored** from the body for the kit's whole life, not borrowed per call, so it is never null while the body is on stage — but it can still be parentless, which is exactly why `canWorldFx` and not `sprite != null` is the gate. `EchoKitBorrow` now lends only `pos`.

The kit itself is **private** on `EchoActionContext`. Reach it through `ctx.gear()` (inventory) or `ctx.stats()` (base-game math that will only take a `Hero`). Never pass `ctx.stats()` to world or VFX code — use `ctx.showEnchant(item)`, `ctx.attackFx(cell)`, or `ctx.zapFx(cell)`, which always target the body. `EchoKitEscapeTest` fails the build on `stats().sprite` and on `Enchanting.show`/`MagicMissile.boltFromChar`/`Flare.show` given the kit.

Relocates: `Char.move(cell, false)` or `ScrollOfTeleportation.appear` — not `pos` alone.

## Tests

Prefer proving Echo VFX with a live parent — skill `echo-combat-vfx-test`:
`installEchoBossLevel` + `attachInstantProjectileParent`, then assert recycles / stub counters.

Headless (no parent) must still apply gameplay synchronously.

